# ── Google service-account credentials — never commit ────────────────
# A service-account JSON is a permanent, non-expiring credential. It is
# downloaded once, cannot be re-downloaded, and grants whatever the
# account can reach until somebody revokes it. It belongs in a Vercel
# environment variable, never in the repository.
#
# There is no single filename to catch: the Cloud Console names the
# download <project-id>-<12 hex>.json, Firebase names it
# <project>-firebase-adminsdk-<id>.json, and people rename both to
# things like credentials.json. So this matches the shapes people
# actually end up with — and deliberately never matches *.json, which
# would swallow package.json, vercel.json and site.webmanifest.
#
# Filename matching is the second line of defence, not the first:
# build.py refuses to finish if a private key or a service_account
# blob reaches the bundle. Spelled out in several casings because
# .gitignore is case-sensitive on Linux and not on macOS.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
service-account*.json
service_account*.json
serviceAccount*.json
ServiceAccount*.json
serviceaccount*.json
google-credentials*.json
google-service-account*.json
gcp-key*.json
client_secret*.json
credentials.json
secrets/
# base64 blob produced when pasting the credential into Vercel
*.b64
